# Wireframe: Issue Detail

## Purpose & Flow Context

The Issue Detail view shows a single issue with its full description, status, assignee, comments, and metadata — updating in real-time as other team members modify the issue or add comments via WebSocket events. Entry: user clicks an IssueCard from the IssueList. Exit: user navigates back to list, or to another issue. This wireframe covers the detail-level layout and how real-time events (status changes, comment additions, field updates from other users) manifest on this screen.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Content area spans 8 columns, metadata sidebar spans 4.

**App-shell**: Shared header + nav + container. Issue Detail sits in the main content area.

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Shared app-shell header | See header-connection-status.wireframes |
| Breadcrumb | "Issues > Issue Title" | Navigation back to list |
| Issue Header | StatusCycleIndicator, Title, Priority | Top of content area |
| Issue Description | Full description text | Main content, scrollable |
| Comment Thread | List of comments with avatars and timestamps | Below description |
| Comment Input | Text input + Submit button | Bottom of comment thread |
| Metadata Sidebar | Status, Assignee, Priority, Labels, Created, Updated | Right side, 4 columns |

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]   [Issues]  [Projects]  [Cycles]  [● Connected] [🔔] [👤] |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Issues > Fix login timeout issue                                 |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                          |                        |
|  ○ Fix login timeout issue               |  Status  [>Todo ▼]    |
|                                          |  Assignee [👤 Sarah ▼] |
|  Users are experiencing a 30-second      |  Priority [>Urgent ▼]  |
|  timeout when attempting to login with    |  Labels   [BUG]        |
|  SSO credentials. This affects all        |                        |
|  enterprise customers using Okta.         |  Created  Jan 15       |
|                                          |  Updated  2m ago       |
|  Steps to reproduce:                     |                        |
|  1. Navigate to login page               |                        |
|  2. Click "Sign in with SSO"             |                        |
|  3. Enter Okta credentials               |                        |
|  4. Observe 30s timeout                  |                        |
|                                          |                        |
|  --- Comments (3) ---                    |                        |
|                                          |                        |
|  👤 Mike Johnson  2h ago                 |                        |
|  I can reproduce this on Chrome and      |                        |
|  Firefox. Looking into the auth module.  |                        |
|                                          |                        |
|  👤 Sarah Chen  1h ago                   |                        |
|  Found the issue — token refresh is      |                        |
|  blocking the main thread.               |                        |
|                                          |                        |
|  👤 Emily Park  30m ago                  |                        |
|  PR ready for review: #421               |                        |
|                                          |                        |
|  [💬 Add a comment...____________] [Send] |                        |
|                                          |                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Breadcrumb | Link | Click navigates back to issue list | None |
| StatusCycleIndicator | StatusCycleIndicator | Shows issue status, cycles on 'S' key | Real-time update flash |
| Issue Title | Heading (h1) | Displays issue title | Truncates if extremely long |
| Description | Text | Shows full issue description | Markdown rendering, code blocks |
| Comment Thread | List | Shows comments in chronological order | New comments insert at bottom with highlight |
| Comment Input | Input + Button | Submits new comment | Disabled while submitting |
| Status Picker | IssueAssigneeSelector-like dropdown | Changes issue status | Optimistic update |
| Assignee Picker | IssueAssigneeSelector | Changes issue assignee | Optimistic update |
| Priority Picker | Dropdown | Changes issue priority | Optimistic update |
| Labels | Label chips | Shows issue labels | Click to add/remove |

## Data Display

This is a detail view, not a data-dense screen. Content hierarchy:
1. **Issue header** (status + title) — primary, top of scan path
2. **Description** — full context
3. **Comments** — chronological thread
4. **Metadata sidebar** — reference info, right side

**Real-time detail-level behaviour:**
- `issue.statusChanged`: StatusCycleIndicator updates with card-level animation
- `issue.assigned`: Assignee avatar/name updates in sidebar
- `issue.updated`: Description or title may update (highlight changed field)
- `comment.created`: New comment inserts at bottom of thread with brief highlight

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Breadcrumb | Navigation context | "Issues > {Issue Title}" |
| Status Label | Current issue state | "Todo", "In Progress", "Done" |
| Assignee Label | Who is responsible | "Sarah Chen" or "Unassigned" |
| Priority Label | Urgency level | "Urgent", "High", "Medium", "Low" |
| Comment Count | Number of comments | "Comments (3)" |
| Comment Input Placeholder | Suggests action | "Add a comment..." |
| Timestamp | When updated | "2m ago", "1h ago", "Yesterday" |

## States

### Populated (Default)

Full issue detail with description, comments, and metadata.

```
(see Layout Regions sketch above)
```

### Updated (Real-time Event Received)

A real-time event modifies the issue. Changed field highlights briefly; new comments insert at bottom.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                          |                        |
|  ● Fix login timeout issue               |  Status  [>In Progress ▼] | ← STATUS CHANGED (highlighted)
|                                          |  Assignee [👤 Sarah ▼] |
|  Users are experiencing a 30-second      |  Priority [>Urgent ▼]  |
|  timeout when attempting to login with    |  Labels   [BUG]        |
|  SSO credentials.                        |                        |
|                                          |  Created  Jan 15       |
|  --- Comments (4) ---                    |  Updated  just now     | ← UPDATED timestamp
|                                          |                        |
|  👤 Mike Johnson  2h ago                 |                        |
|  ...                                     |                        |
|                                          |                        |
|  👤 Emily Park  30m ago                  |                        |
|  PR ready for review: #421               |                        |
|                                          |                        |
|  👤 Alex Rivera  just now                |  ← NEW COMMENT (highlighted)
|  Merged the fix. Deploying to staging.   |
|                                          |                        |
|  [💬 Add a comment...____________] [Send] |                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
  (real-time event: issue.statusChanged + comment.created —
   status field highlights, new comment inserts with highlight)
```

### Loading (Initial Load)

Skeleton mirrors the populated layout — placeholder bars for title, description, comments, sidebar fields.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                          |                        |
|  [○]  [==== skeleton bar ====]           |  Status  [=======]    |
|                                          |  Assignee [=======]   |
|  [======== skeleton bar ============]   |  Priority [=======]   |
|  [======== skeleton bar ============]   |  Labels   [=======]   |
|  [==== skeleton bar ====]               |                        |
|                                          |  Created  [====]      |
|  --- Comments ---                        |  Updated  [====]      |
|                                          |                        |
|  [👤 skeleton  ====]                     |                        |
|  [======== skeleton bar ============]   |                        |
|  [======== skeleton bar ====]           |                        |
|                                          |                        |
|  [💬 skeleton________________] [Send]    |                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Two-column layout: content (8 col) + metadata sidebar (4 col) |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Metadata sidebar collapses below description |
| Mobile (<768px) | Single column, metadata collapses to compact row, comment input full width |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `main` landmark contains detail; sidebar is `aside` |
| Heading order | h1: Issue title, h2: "Comments" section |
| Reading / Focus order | Top to bottom: Breadcrumb → Title → Description → Comments → Comment input; sidebar is complementary |
| Accessible names | Status picker: aria-label="Change issue status", Assignee picker: aria-label="Change issue assignee", Comment input: aria-label="Add a comment" |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through interactive elements; Enter/Space on status/assignee opens picker |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on all pickers, comment input, send button |
| Focus not Obscured | Sidebar is not sticky; scrolls with content |
| Non-color intent | Status dot + label text, priority icon + label |

## Assumptions

- **Existing screen**: This is an existing detail view receiving real-time updates. The wireframe focuses on real-time-specific behaviour (field highlight on update, new comment insertion).
- **Component reuse**: StatusCycleIndicator and IssueAssigneeSelector are reused from existing wireframes. Their optimistic update behaviour is defined in their respective wireframes.
- **Real-time scope**: Only events affecting the currently-viewed issue are relevant. Events for other issues are handled at the list level (see issue-list.wireframes).
